Karmada is installed successfully.

Register Kubernetes cluster to Karmada control plane.

Register cluster with 'Push' mode

Step 1: Use "karmadactl join" command to register the cluster to Karmada control plane. --cluster-kubeconfig is kubeconfig of the member cluster.
(In karmada)~# MEMBER_CLUSTER_NAME=$(cat ~/.kube/config  | grep current-context | sed 's/: /\n/g'| sed '1d'| tr -d "\"'")
(In karmada)~# karmadactl --kubeconfig /home/runner/work/_temp/omni-group-bench-native-10/data/karmada-apiserver.config  join ${MEMBER_CLUSTER_NAME} --cluster-kubeconfig=$HOME/.kube/config

Step 2: Show members of karmada
(In karmada)~# kubectl --kubeconfig /home/runner/work/_temp/omni-group-bench-native-10/data/karmada-apiserver.config get clusters


Register cluster with 'Pull' mode

Step 1: Create bootstrap token and generate the 'karmadactl register' command which will be used later.
~# karmadactl token create --print-register-command --kubeconfig=/home/runner/work/_temp/omni-group-bench-native-10/data/karmada-apiserver.config
This command will generate a registration command similar to:

karmadactl register 172.18.0.5:5443 --token t8xfio.640u9gp9obc72v5d --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:9cfa542ff48f43793d1816b1dd0a78ad574e349d8f6e005e6e32e8ab528e4244

Step 2: Use the output from Step 1 to register the cluster to the Karmada control plane. 
You need to specify the target member cluster by flag '--kubeconfig'
~# karmadactl register 172.18.0.5:5443 --token t8xfio.640u9gp9obc72v5d --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:9cfa542ff48f43793d1816b1dd0a78ad574e349d8f6e005e6e32e8ab528e4244 --kubeconfig=<path-to-member-cluster-kubeconfig>

Step 3: Show members of Karmada.
~# karmadactl --kubeconfig=/home/runner/work/_temp/omni-group-bench-native-10/data/karmada-apiserver.config get clusters

The karmadactl register command has several optional parameters for setting the properties of the member cluster. For more details, run:

~# karmadactl register --help

